{"id": "EUVD-2026-80815", "enisaUuid": "1a67dd87-7d27-39fa-9e32-5ed6e3734760", "description": "Hippo4j through 1.5.0 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in four ThreadPoolController endpoints that fail to validate the clientAddress parameter. Authenticated attackers can supply arbitrary hostnames and ports to trigger outbound GET requests to internal networks and cloud metadata services.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T14:40:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:22:42", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/opengoofy/hippo4j/issues/1621", "https://github.com/opengoofy/hippo4j", "https://github.com/opengoofy/hippo4j/blob/73124de92e269940bdf44f4534b37a13a36ffd49/hippo4j-server/hippo4j-console/src/main/java/cn/hippo4j/console/controller/ThreadPoolController.java#L123-L179", "https://github.com/opengoofy/hippo4j/blob/73124de92e269940bdf44f4534b37a13a36ffd49/hippo4j-server/hippo4j-auth/src/main/java/cn/hippo4j/auth/config/GlobalSecurityConfig.java#L95-L107", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/hippo4j-through-1.5.0-ssrf-via-clientaddress-parameter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9vwf-fv6w-mmfr", "CVE-2026-92569"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01865369-c68a-3aba-8b57-a821b7304c10", "product": {"name": "hippo4j", "vendor": {"name": "opengoofy"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7efbc694-7bca-3e6a-ac77-e2c094c50a10", "vendor": {"name": "opengoofy"}}], "isExploited": false}